{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'Non.negotiable|invariants|No hidden|No implicit|No assumed' docs/design/datom.world.md; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md | sed -n '425,454p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md | sed -n '969,991p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md | sed -n '1550,1568p'; sed -n '88,117p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc; sed -n '398,428p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc; sed -n '167,187p' test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc; sed -n '66,73p' test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; sed -n '342,363p' test/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"2:description: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\n188:2. Identify invariants.\n   425\t`v5` end at 5) and `v0` takes `T2`. Every operand of every instruction\n   426\tdiffers from R1's, and the register count differs.\n   427\t\n   428\tTwo demonstrated samples are not a theorem, so the claim is narrowed to\n   429\twhat the two allocators' stated rules entail. **Lemma (root result).**\n   430\tFor a body whose root expression is a `:call`, `:ffi-call`, `:define` or\n   431\tstream effect with at least one child: R1 gives the root `T0`\n   432\t(`main-temp`, `:380-383`; the lambda bodies' first `allocate-temp!`,\n   433\t`:388`); under §8.2 the root's first child's chain begins at the body's\n   434\tfirst pc and takes `T0`, its interval ends at the root's pc (the root\n   435\treads it) and has not expired there (`end < p` is false), so the root\n   436\tcannot take `T0`. The result register differs. **Lemma (call\n   437\tdestination).** For a `:call` whose operator's first instruction is at\n   438\tthe body's first pc: R1 assigns the call's destination before the\n   439\toperator, so destination < operator slot; §8.2 assigns it at the call's\n   440\tpc while the operator (`T0`) is live, so destination > operator slot.\n   441\tBoth lemmas follow from the two allocation orders alone; conditional and\n   442\t`:resume` roots are **not** covered (for `(if c 1 2)` both allocators\n   443\tgive the result `T0`, since the test interval expires at the\n   444\t`:branch-false`), and no claim is made about them beyond the gate.\n   445\t\n   446\tApplied to the B0 corpus (`parity_test.cljc:39-115`): ten rows are a\n   447\tsingle atom and agree (the six literal rows, `\"closure value\"`, `\"store\n   448\tput then get\"`, `\"gensym\"`, `\"stream make\"`); fourteen rows are\n   449\tcall-rooted and differ by the root lemma; the two `if` rows have a call\n   450\tas test whose operator is at pc 0 and differ by the call-destination\n   451\tlemma. Sixteen of twenty-six differ. Over the register corpus\n   452\t(`corpus.cljc:54-118`) `:literal`, `:variable` and `:stream-make-default`\n   453\tare atoms and agree; every call-rooted row differs by the root lemma; the\n   454\tconditional-rooted rows (`:if`, `:if-in-test`, `:nested-if-same-rd`,\n   969\t     (`prelude.cljc:3395-3414`, a lexical walk over the map AST);\n   970\t   - discharged: `(set (keys (:primitives spec)))` =\n   971\t     `(scan/free-names v4)` minus `(conj (prelude/defined-keys ast) 'yin/def)`\n   972\t     (`prelude.cljc:3416-3425`) minus every name whose namespace symbol\n   973\t     is in the spec's `:requires` keys (`py`, `pym.<i>`). For `py` the\n   974\t     requirement set is empty and this reduces to what\n   975\t     `module-spec-declares-every-free-name-test` checks\n   976\t     (`linked_prelude_test.cljc:167-187`).\n   977\t\n   978\tThe tree oracles are the permanent ones: `vm/free-names`,\n   979\t`ast-requirements`, the `ast-format` scanners and the emission walk are\n   980\tAST-level and survive cutover.\n   981\t\n   982\t### 6.4 \"Old scanner\" after cutover: pinning goldens\n   983\t\n   984\t**PROPOSED.** Phase 8 deletes `yin.vm.linearize`, `yin.vm.code`'s stack\n   985\ttable and the `\"v3\"` scanners with them (frozen §9 \"Rewrite\"). Before\n   986\tthat, slice 5c writes **one golden fixture**\n   987\t`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/scanner_goldens.cljc`: for every program\n   988\tof corpora 1 and 2 and every C4 module of corpus 3, by name, the map\n   989\t`{:free-names #{…} :occurrences [[name in-body?] …] :definitions [[name conditional?] …]\n   990\t:application-count n :requirements {…} :join {:status … …}}` (the join\n   991\tas §6.3 (iii) normalises it, refusals included) as the `\"v3\"` scanners\n  1550\t> **the dependency-closure scanners (UCF §7.6.1) reimplemented over the\n  1551\t> new table answer identically to the old ones on the C4 linked-prelude\n  1552\t> corpus** (free names, store footprint, discharged bodies), since the\n  1553\t> C4 track's module layout is built against those answers.\n  1554\t\n  1555\twith:\n  1556\t\n  1557\t> **the dependency-closure scanners (UCF §7.6.1) reimplemented over the\n  1558\t> new table answer identically to the old ones and to the tree-side\n  1559\t> oracle on the B0 corpus, the register corpus and the C4 linked-prelude\n  1560\t> modules by name** (free-name sets; free-name occurrences and\n  1561\t> definitions compared by name and `:in-body?`/`:conditional?` flag in\n  1562\t> order, positions excluded since the layouts differ; application-site\n  1563\t> counts; store keys, FFI ops, parked ids and effect kinds; and the\n  1564\t> step-5a join's retained obligations in order), with the old scanners'\n  1565\t> answers pinned as goldens before cutover deletes them, since the C4\n  1566\t> track's module declarations are built against those answers.\n  1567\t\n  1568\t### F12 — the frozen §8.1 is unaffected; the structural slot is retired with §8.2\n(defn- fresh-body-ctx\n  [locals]\n  {:code (atom []),\n   :free (atom (sorted-set)),\n   :next-temp (atom 0),\n   :peak (atom 0),\n   :labels (atom {}),\n   :label-count (atom 0),\n   :locals locals})\n\n\n(defn- allocate-temp!\n  \"Lowest-available temp index: the lowest freed index if one exists, else\n   the next never-used index.\"\n  [ctx]\n  (let [free @(:free ctx)]\n    (if (seq free)\n      (let [i (first free)]\n        (swap! (:free ctx) disj i)\n        i)\n      (let [i @(:next-temp ctx)]\n        (reset! (:next-temp ctx) (inc i))\n        (swap! (:peak ctx) max (inc i))\n        i))))\n\n\n(defn- free-temp!\n  [ctx i]\n  (swap! (:free ctx) conj i))\n\n                  descs)\n            lengths (mapv (comp count :code) local-resolved)\n            starts (vec (reductions + 0 lengths))\n            offset-tuple (fn [body-i [_e t]]\n                           (case (nth t 0)\n                             :jump (assoc t 1 (+ (nth t 1) (nth starts body-i)))\n                             :branch-false\n                             (assoc t 2 (+ (nth t 2) (nth starts body-i)))\n                             :closure (assoc t 3 (nth starts (inc (nth t 3))))\n                             t))\n            indexed (map-indexed vector local-resolved)\n            instructions\n            (into []\n                  (mapcat (fn [[i lr]] (map #(offset-tuple i %) (:code lr))))\n                  indexed)\n            sources\n            (into []\n                  (mapcat (fn [[_i lr]] (map first (:code lr))))\n                  indexed)\n            bodies (mapv (fn [i {:keys [locals registers]}]\n                           {:locals locals,\n                            :registers registers,\n                            :start (nth starts i),\n                            :end (dec (nth starts (inc i)))})\n                         (range (count local-resolved)) local-resolved)\n            pre-image {:bodies bodies, :instructions instructions}\n            live-instructions (fill-live pre-image)\n            image {:bodies bodies, :instructions live-instructions}]\n        {:image image,\n         :side-table (register-side-table live-instructions sources\n                                          source params)}))))\n(deftest module-spec-declares-every-free-name-test\n  (let [declared (keys (:primitives (prelude/module-spec registry)))]\n    (testing \"the qualified declarations are exactly the host names (I7)\"\n      (is (= prelude/host-names (set (filter namespace declared)))))\n    (testing \"the bare declarations are primitives\"\n      (is (every? #(contains? vm/primitives %) (remove namespace declared))))\n    (testing \"the exports are no primitive and all defined at module level\"\n      (is (empty? (filter #(contains? vm/primitives %)\n                          prelude/module-exports)))\n      (is (every? (module-level-keys prelude/module-uast)\n                  prelude/module-exports)))\n    (testing \"the runtime keys are what the generated py/init! defines,\n              the ready flag aside\"\n      (is (= (set prelude/runtime-keys)\n             (disj (sexp-def-keys (get (into {} prelude/definitions)\n                                       'py/init!))\n                   'py.rt/state)))\n      (is (= 65 (count prelude/runtime-keys))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n(def published-pysp\n  \"`pysp` published once into `py`'s own content store, which its pinned\n   requirement already lives in: the same shape as `published`.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [{:keys [store address]} @published\n          result (publish/publish-module!\n                   store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) address))]\n      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result)})))\n                    [name (:address\n                            (h/publish-guest-module!\n                              (lower/module-spec reg pk\n                                                 {:name name,\n                                                  :py-address py,\n                                                  :deps deps})))])\n          [_ k-a] (publish \"k\" programs/k-packet {})\n          [_ m-a] (publish \"m\" programs/m-packet {})\n          [_ t-a] (publish \"t\" programs/t-packet {\"k\" k-a})\n          [_ w-a] (publish \"w\" programs/w-packet {})\n          [_ e-a] (publish \"e\" programs/e-packet {})\n          [_ n-a] (publish \"n\" programs/n-packet {})]\n      {:k k-a, :m m-a, :t t-a, :w w-a, :e e-a, :n n-a})))\n\n\n(defn- guest-source\n  \"The serving composition over py and every published guest module.\"\n  []\n  (let [a @published-guests]\n    (h/source (into {'py (:address @h/published)}\n                    (map (fn [[n a]] [(lower/module-symbol (name n)) a]))\n                    a))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
